#: processes/materialize-remote.bpmn:120
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A copy with no expiry cannot be told from an abandoned one — the same argument bean-blocking makes about a block with no expiry. An ARCHIVAL copy is the exception and it is a specification rather than an omission: freshness() reports it `permanent`, not `no-expiry`."
msgstr ""

#: processes/materialize-remote.bpmn:164
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A refusal is not a failure of the process — it is the process working. The node stays `referenced`, which means the graph still knows it exists and where, and the refusing gate's basis is recorded so the next caller does not re-litigate it."
msgstr ""

