#: processes/materialize-remote.bpmn:145
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Fetch, then record sha256 and byte count. Fixity is REQUIRED for an archival copy: an archive that cannot demonstrate it is unchanged is a copy, and it cannot be re-fetched to check, because the thing it would be re-fetched from is what it exists to survive. The data already exists — every structure.json carries sha256 and bytes, and nothing reads them as fixity."
msgstr ""

#: processes/materialize-remote.bpmn:139
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Have all five gates been answered, with none refusing? `yes` fetches the copy and records its fixity; `no, or unknown` leaves the source `referenced` and records why. An unanswered gate counts as a refusal."
msgstr ""

